    <rdfs:label>Joint Filing Agreement</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition>A Joint Filing Agreement is an agreement between parties that allows them to file certain documents jointly, especially with regulatory agencies. Often seen in securities law, it signifies that the filers have collaborated on the document but may not agree on all points or share the same views.</skos:definition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <ns1:contractFamily xml:lang="en">M&amp;A / Transactional</ns1:contractFamily>
  </rdf:Description>
