    <rdfs:label>Obligation of Contracts Clause Claim</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition>An Obligation of Contracts Clause claim is a legal argument asserting that a law or government action violates the Obligation of Contracts Clause of the United States Constitution by impairing the obligations of existing contracts, without a legitimate public purpose, thereby infringing on the sanctity and enforceability of contractual rights.</skos:definition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
