    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="N9ca437bddaae437583639a28f6d1867a"/>
    <rdfs:label>Retention Agreement</rdfs:label>
    <ns1:contractFamily xml:lang="en">Employment &amp; Labour</ns1:contractFamily>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:definition>A Retention Related Agreement is a legally binding contract between an employer and an employee, often a key or high-value employee, with the aim of retaining the employee within the company for a specified period. This type of agreement typically includes provisions for financial incentives, such as bonuses or stock options, and may also outline conditions or obligations the employee must meet to receive these incentives. The primary goal is to encourage employee loyalty and discourage them from leaving the organization during a critical period.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RC7JwUqtsjZFGHqbObFiwBk">
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="zh-cn">干扰尸体</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-mx">Intervención en un cadáver</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="ja-jp">死体損壊罪</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="hi-in">मृत शरीर के साथ हस्तक्षेप</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-es">Intervención en un cadáver</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="pt-br">Violação de cadáver</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="he-il">התערבות עם גופה של מת</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr-fr">Profanation de cadavre</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="de-de">Störung der Totenruhe</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en-gb">Interference with a Dead Body</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:prefLabel>Tortious Interference with a Dead Body</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:definition>The concept of "Interference with a Dead Body" refers to the intentional or negligent disturbance, removal, or destruction of a deceased person's remains, which can result in civil liability for the responsible party.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RCcQHyZbjBHsXsm0zrZGme5"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="N6880dbc86dfd4a60a54128f96981fa23"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RDm4nVQ4Ad7tXBBYvbjqI2I"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label>Interference with a Dead Body</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RVoruROtalNTiniXRiHcxG">
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-mx">Reclamación de cláusula de guerra</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="zh-cn">战争条款索赔</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="de-de">Kriegsklauselanspruch</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en-gb">War Clause Claim</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="ja-jp">戦争条項請求</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr-fr">Réclamation de clause de guerre</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="pt-br">Reivindicação de cláusula de guerra</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="hi-in">युद्ध शर्त दावा</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="he-il">תביעת סעיף מלחמה</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-es">Reclamación de cláusula de guerra</skos:altLabel>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RDkqXQLaqeFlhG4isnkHJuv"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:definition>A War Clause claim is a legal argument asserting that a particular action or law exceeds the constitutional authority granted to the government in times of war. This claim is based on the interpretation that the War Clause, which grants Congress the power to declare war, also imposes limitations on the government's actions during war, such as the exercise of certain powers or the infringement of individual rights.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label>War Clause Claim</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="Nb41bfa024450401294775a5bed949289">
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://staram.in/ontology/contracts#hasEssentialClause"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://staram.in/ontology/contracts#Assignability"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/f1BPS-gjRYOSkEykotZZIQ">
    <skos:definition>This industry comprises establishments known and licensed as general medical and surgical hospitals primarily engaged in providing diagnostic and medical treatment (both surgical and nonsurgical) to inpatients with any of a wide variety of medical conditions. These establishments maintain inpatient beds and provide patients with food services that meet their nutritional requirements. These hospitals have an organized staff of physicians and other medical staff to provide patient care services. These establishments usually provide other services, such as outpatient services, anatomical pathology services, diagnostic X-ray services, clinical laboratory services, operating room services for a variety of procedures, and pharmacy services.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label>General Medical and Surgical Hospitals</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://www.naics.com/six-digit-naics/?code=622110"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/SUmrcq7pTO2nkqVbWbPoJw"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="N0bf1db0851974b7e92475afbe5c51c1f">
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RCp6PzHvkRv1l3pXC9E4Mse"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://staram.in/ontology/contracts#hasEssentialClause"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
