    <skos:altLabel>IRA</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:definition>An Investors' Rights Agreement (IRA) is a legal document that delineates the rights, privileges, and protections afforded to investors, particularly those investing in private companies. It often includes provisions concerning information rights, anti-dilution protections, and registration rights, among others, aimed at protecting the investors' interests and ensuring they have access to critical information.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition>The Investors' Rights Agreement is an arrangement between an issuer and either a subset or all of its stockholders. This agreement delineates mutual rights and obligations concerning key corporate actions that impact stockholders. These actions could include: (1) registering the company's Common Stock, (2) disclosing specific information to stockholders, (3) granting stockholders the right to partake in future equity offerings, and (4) mandating that the issuer notify stockholders about upcoming public offering registrations.</skos:definition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <ns1:contractFamily xml:lang="en">Debt &amp; Credit</ns1:contractFamily>
    <rdfs:label>Investors' Rights Agreement</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
