    <skos:definition>A Commitment Letter is a formal, written document from a lender that outlines the terms under which the lender agrees to provide a loan to a borrower. The letter specifies important details like the loan amount, interest rate, and repayment terms, and it often requires the borrower's acceptance to become binding.</skos:definition>
    <ns1:contractFamily xml:lang="en">Debt &amp; Credit</ns1:contractFamily>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label>Commitment Letter</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
