    <skos:altLabel>Supplementary Agreement</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:definition>A Side Letter is a legal document that supplements a primary contract or agreement, usually to make amendments, grant exceptions, or specify additional terms for a particular party. Unlike amendments that change the main contract for all parties, a side letter typically applies to specific arrangements between two parties within the broader agreement's context.</skos:definition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label>Side Letter</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
