    <skos:definition>An indemnification and hold harmless clause is a contractual provision in which one party agrees to protect and defend another party against any claims or losses arising from a particular transaction or relationship, and to assume all liability for any damages or costs incurred as a result.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
