  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R9SJQGEqTv7Yi81AtSftq1C">
    <rdfs:label>inv_payment_terms</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition>"Discount applied to the invoice if it is paid within the stated number of days. ""10.00/30"" would indicate that the firm will accept a 10% discount of inv_total_net_due if paid within 30 days of the invoice_date.  CAN NOT be used if any tax is charged against any matter/invoice that is part of this inv_id because there may be a legal requirement that the tax amount charged should not be modified.  
  
Law firm can not apply this reduction to the invoice because it is dependent on the payment turnaround by the client; represents an additional discount that must be applied by the client's accounts payable system or third party e-billing vendor if the payment terms are met.
"</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RHfeijrOTjaF7qpuoGIGkR"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RCprumIOHXaOGlie4FV3h7m">
    <skos:altLabel>Unitranche Facility</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel>Blended Debt Facility</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel>Single-Tranche Financing</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:definition>A Unitranche Debt Arrangement is a hybrid financing structure that combines senior and subordinated debt into a single loan facility. This simplifies the borrowing process for the borrower by offering one blended interest rate and one set of loan terms, providing both flexibility and efficiency in managing debt.</skos:definition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:prefLabel>Unified Debt Structure</skos:prefLabel>
    <rdfs:label>Unitranche Debt Arrangement</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RfuC0yNDKhOWj8FHvjuYyg"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RCC22bPzCCS3PR1Q5hBr7PO">
    <skos:prefLabel>Gaming Law</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en-gb">Gaming Law</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-mx">Ley de Juegos de Azar</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="ja-jp">ゲーミング法</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="he-il">חוק המשחקים</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="pt-br">Direito dos jogos</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="zh-cn">博彩法</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel>Gaming Law</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-es">Ley de Juegos de Azar</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr-fr">Droit des jeux</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="de-de">Glücksspielrecht</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="hi-in">जुआ कानून</skos:altLabel>
    <dc:source>Integrated from add/ ontology files on 2026-07-07; add/Law.json</dc:source>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="N26d620f332024084850150a186910612"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RSYBzf149Mi5KE0YtmpUmr"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:hiddenLabel>GAME</skos:hiddenLabel>
    <skos:definition>Law, rules, and regulations that apply to the gaming or gambling industry.</skos:definition>
    <ns2:legacyIdentifier>http://code.sali.org/v1/LMSS/#AoL-GAME</ns2:legacyIdentifier>
    <rdfs:label>Gaming Law</rdfs:label>
    <dc:identifier>IN-LAW-16</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>GAME</dc:identifier>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RCJ5C096Y1Os0YHlEC3q4Dx">
    <skos:altLabel>Locked Box Date Mechanism</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel>Pre-Determined Price Mechanism</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel>Fixed Price Mechanism</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:example>The Locked Box Mechanism simplifies the transaction by eliminating the need for post-closing adjustments.</skos:example>
    <rdfs:label>Locked Box Pricing</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RBUtAfKXfMN4dku9MsqeFjW"/>
    <skos:definition>Locked Box is a pricing mechanism in M&amp;A transactions where the purchase price is based on the target company's financial statements at a specified historical date, known as the locked box date. From this date to the closing date, the seller is prohibited from extracting value from the company, ensuring price certainty and protecting the buyer against financial deterioration.</skos:definition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/q_lK-UYMSN24qCQ5FPP8sQ">
    <rdfs:label>Office Supplies (except Paper) Manufacturing</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/_Wdrm5x7Rze9MtqOCstr9Q"/>
    <skos:definition>This industry comprises establishments primarily engaged in manufacturing office supplies. Examples of products made by these establishments are pens, pencils, felt tip markers, crayons, chalk, pencil sharpeners, staplers, modeling clay, hand operated stamps, stamp pads, stencils, carbon paper, and inked ribbons.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://www.naics.com/six-digit-naics/?code=339940"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
