    <rdfs:label>Putable Asset</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition>A Putable Asset is a financial instrument that grants the holder the right to sell the asset back to the issuer at a specified price before its maturity date. This feature provides investors with the flexibility to exit the investment under certain conditions, often mitigating potential losses and reducing risk.</skos:definition>
