  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R7Rdvjz7Q76QLZXnSJ66z40">
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en-gb">M&amp;A Transactional Method</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="he-il">שיטת עסקאות M&amp;A</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="ja-jp">M&amp;Aトランザクション手法</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="hi-in">एम एंड ए ट्रांजैक्शनल मैथड</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="de-de">M&amp;A-Transaktionsmethode</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr-fr">Méthode transactionnelle M&amp;A</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="zh-cn">并购交易方法</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="pt-br">Método transacional de M&amp;A</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel>M&amp;A Deal Structure</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-es">Método Transaccional de M&amp;A</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-mx">Método Transaccional de M&amp;A</skos:altLabel>
    <rdfs:label>M&amp;A Transactional Method</rdfs:label>
    <dc:source>ABA M&amp;A Deal Points Study</dc:source>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RDRCaFxX4hpUklgNnVS9D8C"/>
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://public.tableau.com/app/profile/the.atticus.project/viz/ABADealPointsStudy/Home"/>
    <skos:definition>A M&amp;A Deal Structure is the specific plan or arrangement for the merger or acquisition of companies, including the methods used to acquire the target company, such as tender offers or mergers, and the legal framework supporting the execution of the plan.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R7dcZJLuYutSG7vbZRwstAC">
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr-fr">Réclamation en vertu de la loi californienne sur les droits de la famille</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="he-il">תביעה על פי חוק זכויות המשפחה של קליפורניה</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en-gb">California Family Rights Act Claim</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="ja-jp">カリフォルニア家族権利法クレーム</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="hi-in">कैलिफोर्निया परिवार अधिकार अधिनियम दावा</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="de-de">Anspruch nach dem kalifornischen Familienrechtsakt</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="pt-br">Reivindicação da Lei de Direitos da Família da Califórnia</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="zh-cn">加利福尼亚家庭权利法索赔</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-mx">Reclamo de la Ley de Derechos Familiares de California</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel>CFRA Claim</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-es">Reclamo de la Ley de Derechos Familiares de California</skos:altLabel>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R9LVBKjvGRuzwgtlhuLST36"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="N7d68f2571cc745d6acd503f5ebf5ef6d"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="N5255ef497a094dd292ee8f18a9e63e54"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RCty0MaQzrLC9KnzjM7nMER"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R9UYGSnWQz2MvNsWUofGb6J"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="N2585d61b9c034ef4b0c2bca75604060c"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label>California Family Rights Act Claim</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition>A California Family Rights Act (CFRA) claim is a legal action initiated by an employee against their employer for not complying with the CFRA, which provides eligible employees with up to 12 weeks of unpaid leave in a 12-month period for certain family or medical reasons, such as the birth or adoption of a child, the employee's own serious health condition, or to care for a seriously ill family member. The claim typically arises when an employer denies an employee's request for CFRA leave or interferes with an employee's right to take CFRA leave, or retaliates against an employee for exercising their right to CFRA leave. Employers can face liability for violating the CFRA, which can result in significant damages for the affected employee.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
