    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:definition>A Successors and Assigns Clause is a provision in a contract that allows the rights and obligations of the parties to be transferred to another person or entity in the event of a merger, acquisition, or other change in ownership.</skos:definition>
