    <skos:definition>A Qualified Income Offset Clause is a provision in a contract that allows for the reduction of one party's income by the amount of benefits received by the other party, typically in the context of divorce or separation agreements.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label>Qualified Income Offset Clause</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
