    <skos:definition>A Prime Brokerage Agreement is a contract between a prime brokerage firm and a client, usually a large institutional investor such as a hedge fund, wherein the firm agrees to provide a range of services. These services often include securities lending, leveraged trade execution, cash management, and custodial services, tailored to support the client's investment operations and risk management strategies.</skos:definition>
    <skos:altLabel>Prime Brokerage Services Agreement</skos:altLabel>
    <rdfs:label>Prime Brokerage Agreement</rdfs:label>
    <ns1:contractFamily xml:lang="en">Investment &amp; Financial Services</ns1:contractFamily>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
