    <rdfs:label>Bermudan Call Option Style</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition>A Bermudan Call Option Style is a type of option contract that can be exercised on specific dates during its life, typically more than one date but fewer than the continuous exercise rights of American options. This style offers a middle ground between the flexibility of American options and the strict single-date exercise of European options.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R8nvlmwJzNQu4OM3ZwpWBjM">
    <skos:definition>"Immigration Process Modifications" encompass actions such as amendments, renewals, and extensions within the immigration process, where changes are made to existing immigration applications or statuses, allowing individuals to update, extend, or renew their legal presence or rights within the destination country. These actions usually involve submitting necessary documents and obtaining approval from immigration authorities.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label>Immigration Process Modifications</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R9ODLnhxFt38FQNV4BUbRSD"/>
  </rdf:Description>
