  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RDaOGV6LGc4JwU1Wti93rFn">
    <skos:altLabel>Scenic and Sightseeing Transportation</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="zh-cn">风景和观光运输业</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="pt-br">Indústria de transporte cênico e turístico</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="de-de">Industrie für landschaftliche und touristische Transporte</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="ja-jp">景観・観光輸送業</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr-fr">Industrie du transport touristique et panoramique</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:definition>Industries in this group utilize transportation equipment to provide recreation and entertainment. These activities have a production process distinct from passenger transportation carried out for the purpose of other types of for-hire transportation. transport may be by ground, air, rail water or other means. This process does not emphasize efficient transportation; in fact, such activities often use obsolete vehicles, such as steam trains, to provide some extra ambiance.</skos:definition>
    <dc:identifier>TRA-SCET</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>IN-INDUSTRY-18.6</dc:identifier>
    <ns2:legacyIdentifier>http://code.sali.org/v1/LMSS/#Ind-TRA-SCET</ns2:legacyIdentifier>
    <skos:hiddenLabel>SCET</skos:hiddenLabel>
