    <rdfs:label>Medical Provider Liability to Third Parties</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition>The legal responsibility of a medical provider to compensate third parties for harm caused by their actions or omissions, including situations where the provider is not directly at fault but may be held liable under agency or vicarious liability principles.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
