  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://staram.in/ontology/epc">
    <vann:preferredNamespaceUri>https://staram.in/ontology/epc#</vann:preferredNamespaceUri>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://staram.in/ontology/epc#SourceModule"/>
    <dcterms:title xml:lang="en">EPC Contract Risk Ontology (Core / TBox)</dcterms:title>
    <dcterms:license xml:lang="en">To be determined by STARAM</dcterms:license>
    <vann:preferredNamespacePrefix>epc</vann:preferredNamespacePrefix>
    <owl:versionInfo>https://staram.in/ontology/epc/0.1.0</owl:versionInfo>
    <dcterms:description xml:lang="en">A core vocabulary for representing risk in Engineering, Procurement and
Construction (EPC) contracts and in the tender / NIT documents that precede them.

The ontology distinguishes two things that are routinely conflated in practice:
  (a) a RISK HEAD - a reusable, contract-independent archetype of a drafting or
      allocation defect (e.g. 'Concurrent Delay Treatment Silent'), maintained in a
      register and used as a review checklist; and
  (b) a RISK FINDING - the observation of such a risk in one identified document
      component of one identified contract, together with the party who bears it,
      the relief (if any) available, and the instrument that backs it.

Allocation is modelled twice on purpose: as a reified epc:RiskAllocation node
(carrying clause + role + pattern + relief + instrument + qualification) and as
shortcut object properties derived from it through owl:propertyChainAxiom, so that
simple queries stay simple without loss of n-ary detail.</dcterms:description>
    <dcterms:created rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-08-12</dcterms:created>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Alignment axioms to https://staram.in/ontology/mact-folio-integrated are kept in a separate module (epc-alignment-mact-folio.ttl) and are NOT imported here, pending confirmation of that namespace's terms.</rdfs:comment>
  </rdf:Description>
