    <skos:prefLabel>Poison Pill</skos:prefLabel>
    <rdfs:label>Shareholder Rights Plan</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <ns1:contractFamily xml:lang="en">Corporate Governance &amp; Formation</ns1:contractFamily>
    <skos:definition>A Shareholder Rights Plan, which is often called a "poison pill," is a defensive strategy employed by corporations to deter hostile takeovers. This plan gives existing shareholders the right to buy additional shares at a discount, thus diluting the potential acquirer's stake.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R9rnG4wClyq3rqQhnwAMqOA">
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="he-il">שימוש ומגורים בלעדיים</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en-gb">Exclusive Use and Occupancy</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="de-de">Ausschließliche Nutzung und Besetzung</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-mx">Uso y ocupación exclusivos</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="ja-jp">独占的使用と占有</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="zh-cn">独占使用和占有</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="hi-in">अनन्य उपयोग और आवास</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-es">Uso y ocupación exclusivos</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="pt-br">Uso e ocupação exclusivos</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr-fr">Usage et occupation exclusifs</skos:altLabel>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RCQJU54O6qCvotCfmDwYZwj"/>
    <skos:definition>The concept of Exclusive Use and Occupancy refers to a legal remedy sought by one spouse in a matrimonial emergency application, which allows them to have sole possession and control of the matrimonial home, excluding the other spouse.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label>Exclusive Use and Occupancy</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RDcQ2WqIyuInoKQbithTsL2">
    <dc:source>Fed. R. Evid. 611</dc:source>
    <dc:source>Fed. R. Evid. 403</dc:source>
    <skos:altLabel>Repetitious Objection</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel>Repetitive Evidence Objection</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel>Redundant Evidence Objection</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel>Asked and Answered Objection</skos:altLabel>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label>Cumulative Objection</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition>An Objection to Cumulative Evidence is raised when a party in a legal proceeding believes that the evidence being presented is repetitive and does not add any new information to the case. This objection aims to prevent the unnecessary prolongation of the proceeding and to avoid undue emphasis on certain evidence.</skos:definition>
    <skos:prefLabel>Objection to Repetitious Evidence</skos:prefLabel>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R7NB9WJzAFK6tIIGmfIj5Ay"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RBMlUtTtbQUQxrZrkeF8Fpm"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/iRMo1yJkTOOh2tWGMHrz2g">
