    <skos:definition>A Negotiable Instrument Forged or Stolen Claim is a legal claim related to a written promise to pay a specific amount of money that has been fraudulently created or taken without authorization, and is related to banking, commercial paper, and creditor claims.</skos:definition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label>Negotiable Instrument Forged or Stolen Claim</rdfs:label>
