  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/Rx7CkM9fjahTS5lZtG21ZR">
    <skos:prefLabel>Property Use</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:definition>Occupancy refers to the act of residing in or using a property or space. This includes the possession and control of the property, typically under a lease or ownership agreement, and entails responsibilities such as maintenance and adherence to property regulations. Occupancy refers to the physical act of living in or using a property, which can be temporary or intermittent, in contrast to "residence," which refers to a person's fixed, permanent, and principal home, often with legal implications and the intention to remain for an extended period.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="N03868d932e234db9ba7d9cc32d86d0f3"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R8nREeU6lB0zs0dt9N339nm"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label>Occupancy</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
