    <rdfs:label>Breach of Contract for Failure to Perform</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RekH7Y6qcTZ3UyrEWZlQK">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RCzQzQSPRAB9cLkvDtBJFn"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:definition>These rights pertain to the use of water from sources that exist on the surface of the land, such as lakes, rivers, and streams. The allocation and usage of these rights can be based on factors like historic use, regional laws, and treaties.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label>Surface Water Rights</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RBXa7Zas4KaZjtUpwq0RHxv">
    <skos:definition>The Natural Law System is a legal philosophy asserting that laws are derived from a set of inherent moral principles and universal truths that govern human behavior, existing independently of human-made laws. It posits that these principles are discoverable through reason and are inherent to human nature, providing a basis for evaluating and guiding positive law.</skos:definition>
    <skos:altLabel>Natural Law Theory</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel>Jus Naturale</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel>Law of Nature</skos:altLabel>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:example>Human Rights Charters often draw on principles from the Natural Law System, asserting rights that transcend national legal systems.</skos:example>
    <skos:example>The abolition of apartheid in South Africa was partly justified by appeals to the universal moral principles of the Natural Law System.</skos:example>
    <rdfs:label>Natural Law System</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RVPwUkNgWhlwyYWWSPrLuZ"/>
    <skos:prefLabel>Universal Moral Law</skos:prefLabel>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R9S9syz75j5TGwoRY2DKWvB">
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en-gb">Accord and Satisfaction Clause</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="pt-br">Cláusula de Acordo e Satisfação</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="de-de">Klausel zur Erfüllung und Befriedigung</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr-fr">Clause d'accord et de satisfaction</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="ja-jp">和解および満足条項</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-es">Cláusula de Conformidad y Satisfacción</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-mx">Cláusula de Conformidad y Satisfacción</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="he-il">סעיף הסכמה והפרעה</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="hi-in">अनुबंध और संतोष बंधन धारा</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="zh-cn">和解与满足条款</skos:altLabel>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:definition>An Accord and Satisfaction Clause is a provision in a contract that allows parties to settle a dispute by agreeing to different terms than originally agreed upon.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label>Accord and Satisfaction Clause</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RDe0RKU39BlhcyACJW30ZLc"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R7alL3ThuE851s7NQLQmXZX">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RDe0RKU39BlhcyACJW30ZLc"/>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en-gb">Forfeiture Clause</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="hi-in">फोर्फेचर क्लॉज</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-es">Cláusula de Forfeiture</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="de-de">Verfallsklausel</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr-fr">Clause de déchéance</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-mx">Cláusula de Pérdida</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="ja-jp">没収条項</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="zh-cn">没收条款</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="he-il">סעיף מחילות</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="pt-br">Cláusula de perda</skos:altLabel>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:definition>A forfeiture clause is a provision in a contract that allows one party to forfeit or lose their right to something, such as a deposit, if they fail to meet certain obligations outlined in the contract.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label>Forfeiture Clause</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
