  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/Rey5MjRK7y2McE1mi9DS4D">
    <skos:definition>A Directly or Indirectly Clause is a provision in a contract that either explicitly or implicitly imposes obligations or restrictions on a party, and is a subcategory of a Contractual Clause.</skos:definition>
