  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R9PdcdE8HbgI3sqZloSC6HJ">
    <skos:definition>Antitrust - Vertical Market Allocation Claims refer to legal claims that allege an agreement between competitors to divide a market based on vertical lines, such as by customer type or geographic area, in violation of antitrust laws.</skos:definition>
