  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://staram.in/ontology/epc/taxonomy">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://staram.in/ontology/epc#SourceModule"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <owl:versionInfo>https://staram.in/ontology/epc/taxonomy/0.1.0</owl:versionInfo>
    <dcterms:created rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-08-12</dcterms:created>
    <dcterms:title xml:lang="en">EPC Risk Taxonomies and Controlled Vocabularies</dcterms:title>
    <dcterms:description xml:lang="en">Two SKOS concept schemes plus the controlled vocabularies the core ontology points at.

SCHEME 1 - Legal Review Risk Taxonomy (21 concepts): the Category column of the
Legal Risk Register 200. Its unit of analysis is a DRAFTING DEFECT, assessed before
signature and largely independent of any one project.

SCHEME 2 - Allocation Risk Taxonomy (7 concepts): the categories used in the CH-83
extraction. Its unit of analysis is WHO CARRIES A RISK under an identified clause of
an executed contract, organised by project lifecycle.

The two are kept as separate schemes, not merged, because a merge would silently
assert that a defect category and an allocation category are the same kind of thing.
They are joined only by SKOS mapping properties (closeMatch where the concepts are
near-identical, broadMatch where one subsumes the other, relatedMatch otherwise).
Three of the 21 have no home in the 7 - see epcx:mappingGapNote.</dcterms:description>
  </rdf:Description>
