  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R8TdEzcPmKmlt57CbOAlm7">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:definition>"Not guilty" is a legal determination made by a court in a criminal case when the defendant has been acquitted or found not responsible for the charges brought against them. It indicates that the prosecution failed to prove the defendant's guilt, and as a result, the defendant is not subject to criminal penalties or convictions for the alleged crime.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="Na12250e4fc3a4a94a5b8b1ac1725afe1"/>
