    <skos:definition>Audit practice refers to the systematic process of evaluating and examining an organization's records, processes, operations, and performance — ensuring compliance with laws, standards, and regulations. Audits can relate to many areas of law (e.g., Tax, Employment, Regulatory).</skos:definition>
