    <rdfs:label>Waiver of Subrogation Clause</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition>A Waiver of Subrogation Clause is a provision in a contract where one party agrees to waive their right to seek reimbursement from another party's insurance company for damages covered by the insurance policy.</skos:definition>
