  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RBRZmOHb12gHkQhkd7ml4DC">
    <skos:definition>An Article V claim pertains to a legal argument based on Article V of the U.S. Constitution, which sets out the process for amending the Constitution. Such a claim might arise in disputes over the interpretation or application of the amendment process, including the proposal and ratification of amendments.</skos:definition>
