  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RCv6Kq9tkPBxjujeEY7MyL9">
    <rdfs:label>COMI (Center of Main Interest)</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RDbrzFzgheftqJ09xcT2ICs"/>
    <skos:definition>COMI, or Center of Main Interest, refers to the primary location where a debtor conducts its principal business operations and is recognized as the central point of its economic activities. This concept is crucial in cross-border insolvency cases to determine jurisdiction and the appropriate forum for the main insolvency proceeding.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
