    <rdfs:label>Liquidated Damages</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition>A predetermined amount of damages agreed upon by parties in a contract, to be paid in the event of a breach of the contract, intended to compensate the non-breaching party for losses that are difficult to quantify.</skos:definition>
