  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RCE5Ek48Cc0wk8ZFM1dRhLu">
    <rdfs:label>Subsidy</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R79ZRcChNA1jEORJLsPWYSv"/>
    <skos:definition>A Subsidy is a financial assistance provided by the government to individuals, businesses, or industries to support economic activities deemed beneficial for the public or to reduce the cost of goods and services. Subsidies can take various forms, including direct cash payments, tax breaks, or reduced interest loans, aimed at promoting economic growth, sustainability, and social welfare.</skos:definition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:example>A housing subsidy assists low-income families in affording rental housing or home purchases, enhancing access to affordable housing.</skos:example>
    <skos:example>An energy subsidy supports the development of renewable energy sources by reducing the costs associated with solar, wind, or bioenergy projects.</skos:example>
    <skos:example>An agricultural subsidy helps farmers by providing financial assistance to ensure stable food prices and production.</skos:example>
    <skos:prefLabel>State Aid</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:altLabel>Economic Assistance</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel>Financial Aid</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel>Government Grant</skos:altLabel>
  </rdf:Description>
