    <rdfs:label>First Amendment Defense</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition>A First Amendment Defense is a legal strategy used in both criminal and civil litigation to protect an individual's right to free speech, religion, press, assembly, and petition as guaranteed by the First Amendment of the United States Constitution.</skos:definition>
