    <rdfs:label>Real Estate Zoning Modifications</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition>Real Estate Zoning Modifications refer to changes in the zoning classifications or rules governing the use, development, or characteristics of a specific parcel of land. These modifications are generally initiated by property owners and require approval from local zoning authorities, often after public hearings, assessments, and legal evaluations.</skos:definition>
