    <skos:altLabel>Maximum Risk Exposure</skos:altLabel>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RDsWDLg5JUKHPw6my6QzmoU"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="Nb6fcb8a40f3949b48cc113bc4ca24f42"/>
    <rdfs:label>Risk Capacity</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition>Risk capacity is the maximum amount of legal, financial, operational, or strategic uncertainty that a person or organization can absorb before experiencing existential, catastrophic, or irreversible harm. Unlike risk tolerance, which reflects a decision-maker's willingness to accept uncertainty, risk capacity is determined by objective factors such as available resources, capital reserves, insurance coverage, legal protections, organizational resilience, and the ability to continue functioning after adverse outcomes.</skos:definition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
