    <skos:altLabel>Debt Default</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:definition>A Loan Default occurs when a borrower fails to meet the legal obligations or conditions of a loan agreement, typically involving missed payments or breach of other terms. This default triggers legal consequences and can lead to actions such as foreclosure, repossession, or litigation.</skos:definition>
