    <skos:altLabel>Institutional Bond Offering</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel>Wholesale Debt Sale</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:definition>Institutional Debt Offering refers to the sale of debt securities primarily to institutional investors, such as banks, insurance companies, pension funds, and mutual funds. This method of distribution typically involves larger issuance amounts, more complex underwriting processes, and higher denominations compared to retail debt placements.</skos:definition>
