    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:definition>A "No Default Clause" is a provision in a contract that specifies that neither party can be considered in default unless a specific event or condition occurs, as defined in the contract.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label>No Default Clause</rdfs:label>
