  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RCbrZc9nUSYGtNJnMNow5xS">
    <skos:definition>A Board Secretary, also known as Secretary of the Board, is an officer responsible for managing the administrative tasks of a board of directors, including preparing agendas, recording meeting minutes, and maintaining corporate governance documents. The Secretary ensures compliance with legal and regulatory requirements and facilitates communication between the board and executive management.</skos:definition>
