    <skos:definition>Multi-District Litigation (MDL) refers to a legal procedure where multiple related cases from different jurisdictions are consolidated and transferred to a single court for pretrial proceedings.</skos:definition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
