  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RTVHIHUY48KidG92GXtTlH">
    <skos:definition>In corporate law and business, "has subsidiary" refers to the relationship where a parent company owns and controls a separate and distinct company, known as a subsidiary. This denotes that the subsidiary operates as an independent entity but is under the significant influence or control of the parent corporation, both in management and often in financial matters.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label>hasSubsidiary</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label>sali:hasSubsidiary</rdfs:label>
    <skos:example>Meta hasSubsidiary Facebook</skos:example>
    <skos:example>Alphabet hasSubsidiary Google</skos:example>
    <skos:notation>folio:hasSubsidiary</skos:notation>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <skos:altLabel>has the subsidiary</skos:altLabel>
  </rdf:Description>
