    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RCEDL3kMYgjFUEOhOyGp3IE"/>
    <skos:definition>A co-party in a litigation or transactional matter who, although formally aligned on the same side (such as co-plaintiffs or co-defendants), is acting contrary to the interests of a specific client in the same proceeding or deal. This adverse action may involve conflicting positions, strategies, or goals within the shared matter.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label>Adverse Co-Party</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R8AhhP8gb3fCPRIOJmR3oyD">
    <skos:definition>A criminal agreement between two or more people to commit a crime, even if the crime is never carried out, falls under the concept of Criminal Conspiracy in the field of Inchoate Criminal Offenses and Concert of Action Crimes.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label>Criminal Conspiracy</rdfs:label>
