    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:definition>Governmental Immunity for Condition of Public Property: A legal concept that shields government entities from liability for injuries or damages caused by the condition of public property, unless the government entity failed to take reasonable steps to correct the dangerous condition.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label>Governmental Immunity for Condition of Public Property</rdfs:label>
