    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R49sp0iRvML6Mzkr06Bimd"/>
    <skos:definition>The Insurer's Breach of Implied Covenant of Good Faith and Fair Dealing refers to a violation by an insurance company of the obligation to act in good faith and deal fairly with its policyholders, which is implied in every insurance contract.</skos:definition>
