    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-mx">Condición de cierre de efecto adverso material independiente</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="zh-cn">独立的实质性不利影响结束条件</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr-fr">Condition de clôture d'effet indépendant matériel négatif</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en-gb">Standalone Material Adverse Effect Closing Condition</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="he-il">תנאי סגירה של השפעה שלילית חומרית עצמאית</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="de-de">Bedingung für den Abschluss eines eigenständigen wesentlichen nachteiligen Effekts</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel>MAE</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-es">Condición de cierre de efecto adverso material independiente</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="hi-in">स्वतंत्र सामग्री विपरीत प्रभाव समापन शर्त</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="ja-jp">スタンドアロンマテリアルアドバースエフェクトクロージングコンディション</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="pt-br">Condição de Fechamento de Efeito Adverso Material Independente</skos:altLabel>
    <rdfs:label>Standalone Material Adverse Effect Closing Condition</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <dc:source>ABA M&amp;A Deal Points Study</dc:source>
    <skos:definition>A Standalone Material Adverse Effect (MAE) Closing Condition, also known as MAE, is a specific language used in legal agreements that outlines the circumstances under which a party can terminate the agreement due to a significant negative change in the financial or operational condition of the other party.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R8fcGNgScyMlOAFxW5Omw5Y">
    <skos:prefLabel>Sexual Assault</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:definition>The carnal knowledge of a person, forcibly and/or against that person’s will or not forcibly or against the person’s will in instances where the victim is incapable of giving consent because of his/her temporary or permanent mental or physical incapacity.</skos:definition>
