    <skos:definition>Debarment refers to the exclusion of an individual or entity from participating in certain activities, particularly government contracting and subcontracting, due to violations of regulations, misconduct, or failure to comply with contractual obligations. This measure aims to protect public interest by preventing unreliable or unethical parties from engaging in government-related activities.</skos:definition>
    <skos:prefLabel>Public Procurement Exclusion</skos:prefLabel>
    <rdfs:label>Debarment</rdfs:label>
    <skos:altLabel>Contractor Ban</skos:altLabel>
  </rdf:Description>
