  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R80IXUHvqeO6aI5m9RIDEpB">
    <skos:definition>A Mixed Distribution Fund is an investment fund that allocates its investment profits by partially distributing them to shareholders and partially reinvesting them back into the fund. This balanced approach aims to provide both income and capital growth to investors.</skos:definition>
