  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://staram.in/ontology/legislation#OASISLegislationStructureModule">
    <dcterms:publisher xml:lang="en">Staram</dcterms:publisher>
    <dcterms:created rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-09-10</dcterms:created>
    <rdfs:label>OASIS and Legislation Structure</rdfs:label>
    <skos:note xml:lang="en">ORGANISATIONAL, NOT SEMANTIC. The single rdfs:subClassOf linking this node to 'ZZZ - SANDBOX: UNDER CONSTRUCTION' follows the convention already used by that class's other children; it asserts nothing about legislation. Removing that one triple detaches the entire module and graduates it. Do not build inference on it.</skos:note>
    <skos:note xml:lang="en">Deduplication on ingest: 8 OASIS LegalRuleML metamodel classes and 8 nbfc-compliance individuals (3 statutory authorities, 5 legislative instruments) were reused on their existing Staram base-graph IRIs instead of being minted again. A further 10 base-graph classes are aligned by rdfs:seeAlso rather than collapsed, because the base graph models them as owl:Class where this module models them as NamedIndividual.</skos:note>
    <dcterms:title xml:lang="en">Staram deontic graph - norms across five instruments and one notification, aligned to OASIS LegalRuleML</dcterms:title>
    <dcterms:title xml:lang="en">Staram Indian Legislation Ontology</dcterms:title>
    <owl:versionInfo>1.0.0</owl:versionInfo>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Module root for the Staram deontic graph: a three-layer OWL 2 model of Indian statutory and subordinate legislation. LAYER 1 (Bibliographic/FRBR): abstract Works and their time-bounded Expressions. LAYER 2 (Structural/Akoma Ntoso): the containment hierarchy of a legislative text (Act &gt; Part &gt; Chapter &gt; Rule &gt; Sub-rule &gt; Paragraph) plus annexed material. LAYER 3 (Classification): legal concepts, actors, normative effects and subject domains attached to structural nodes, with provenance and confidence on every machine-derived assertion. The deontic vocabulary is aligned to the OASIS LegalRuleML metamodel classes already held under Standards Compatibility.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:description xml:lang="en">A three-layer OWL 2 ontology for Indian statutory and subordinate legislation.
LAYER 1 (Bibliographic/FRBR): abstract Works and their time-bounded Expressions.
LAYER 2 (Structural/Akoma Ntoso): the physical containment hierarchy of a legislative text
        (Act &gt; Part &gt; Chapter &gt; Rule &gt; Sub-rule &gt; Paragraph), plus annexed material.
LAYER 3 (Classification): the semantic overlay - legal concepts, actors, normative effects and
        subject domains attached to structural nodes, with provenance and confidence on every
        machine-derived assertion.</dcterms:description>
  </rdf:Description>
