  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R8GdwZqxh68i37ND4exqzbh">
    <skos:definition>Originating Country, in the context of immigration and customs, refers to the country from which an individual or goods have moved or are seeking to move from. In the immigration context, this move is often with the intention of settling in another country either temporarily or permanently. This term is important for customs and immigration processes and policies, as it can influence visa requirements, eligibility for asylum, and other legal considerations.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition>Originating Country, in the context of immigration, refers to the country from which an individual has moved or is seeking to move from, often with the intention of settling in another country either temporarily or permanently. This term is important for immigration processes and policies, as it can influence visa requirements, eligibility for asylum, and other legal considerations.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="N6a596c8e36d348b29e07d97f32b7c9b2"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R9ODLnhxFt38FQNV4BUbRSD"/>
    <rdfs:label>Originating Country</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
