  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RDSmGRMaYfZ97elBp5tV28A">
    <skos:definition>A Termination Without Cause Clause is a provision in a contract that allows one party to end the agreement without providing a reason or justification.</skos:definition>
