  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RC3e5wjlKsjPKT8crKFSdIf">
    <skos:definition>Tax Foreclosure is the legal process through which a governmental authority seizes property due to unpaid property taxes. The property is then sold, typically at a public auction, to satisfy the tax debt and any associated penalties or fees</skos:definition>
