    <rdfs:label>Litigation Civil Defenses</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition>Litigation Civil Defenses are legal arguments and strategies used by a party in a civil lawsuit to defend against the claims made by the opposing party, including but not limited to, affirmative defenses, evidentiary defenses, and procedural defenses.</skos:definition>
