  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RC7lPEWMGP3nYZ7PhzT6nbD">
    <skos:definition>A Closed List Party-List Proportional Representation System is an electoral method where voters cast their ballots for a party, and the party determines the order of candidates on its list. Seats are allocated to each party based on the proportion of votes received, and candidates are selected in the predetermined order.</skos:definition>
    <dc:source rdf:resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Closed_list"/>
    <skos:example>Regional Closed List: South Africa's National Assembly elections</skos:example>
    <skos:example>National Closed List: Spain's Congreso de los Diputados elections</skos:example>
    <skos:prefLabel>Party-Determined List System</skos:prefLabel>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RCMZqt2BD3qRRYlj61ssnIZ"/>
    <rdfs:label>Party-List Proportional Representation System - Closed List</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R901IdoFMDxhFpxABCy0UsE">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RB7BB00LuJawNLM8CZW6z7U"/>
    <skos:altLabel>Seeking Advisory Opinion</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:definition>Seeking an advisory judicial opinion involves requesting a court's guidance on a legal question, usually without the existence of an actual case or controversy. Such opinions are generally non-binding and are more common in some legal systems than others; for example, U.S. federal courts generally do not issue advisory opinions due to the "case or controversy" requirement under Article III of the Constitution.</skos:definition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label>Seeking Advisory Judicial Opinion</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
