  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R8cGjHXv3vecVd4ZO6HVjo">
    <skos:definition>"Immigration processing type" refers to the specific stage or procedure within the immigration process, such as visa applications, port of entry checks, change of status requests, or extensions, each with its own requirements and documentation. These steps are crucial for determining an individual's eligibility for entry, residency, or other immigration-related benefits in a destination country.</skos:definition>
