    <rdfs:label>Wrongful Discharge in Violation of Public Policy</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:definition>The concept of "Wrongful Discharge in Violation of Public Policy" refers to the termination of an employee by an employer in a manner that violates public policy, such as firing an employee for refusing to engage in illegal activities or for reporting illegal conduct.</skos:definition>
