    <skos:prefLabel>Driving Without Insurance</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:definition>"Driving Without Insurance" refers to the act of operating a motor vehicle without having the necessary insurance coverage as required by law. This is considered a legal offense in many jurisdictions and may result in penalties, fines, and even suspension of the driver's license.</skos:definition>
