  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RBfYaEPtCAVEbeQxgFszQIc">
    <skos:definition>A Non Circumvention Clause is a provision in a contract that prohibits the parties from bypassing each other and making direct contact or doing business with each other's contacts or associates.</skos:definition>
