    <rdfs:label>Comparative Fault of Others</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:definition>The concept of Comparative Fault of Others refers to the legal principle that allows a defendant to argue that the fault of a non-party contributed to the plaintiff's injuries, and that the damages should be reduced accordingly.</skos:definition>
