    <skos:definition>A government official is an individual who holds a position of authority within a governmental organization, either elected or appointed. Their responsibilities vary widely depending on their role and the level of government they serve, but they are generally tasked with implementing laws, managing public services, and representing the interests of their constituents or the state.</skos:definition>
