    <skos:definition>A Prison Guard is a security officer responsible for maintaining order, enforcing rules, and ensuring the safety of inmates and staff within a correctional facility. They perform duties such as monitoring inmate activities, conducting searches, and responding to emergencies to prevent disturbances and uphold security protocols.</skos:definition>
