    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:definition>A Pedestrian Right-of-Way Violation Claim involves allegations that a driver has failed to yield the right-of-way to pedestrians under circumstances where pedestrians are legally prioritized, such as crosswalks or signals.</skos:definition>
