    <skos:definition>Bias in an AI system refers to the differential treatment of different groups and concepts, which may arise from implicit systems of meaning, norms, and values. Bias can lead to unfair or discriminatory outcomes, impacting the effectiveness and ethical alignment of AI systems.</skos:definition>
