    <rdfs:label>Statutory Deductions Clause</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition>A Statutory Deductions Clause is a provision in a contract that requires the employer to deduct certain amounts from an employee's pay, such as taxes and social security contributions, as required by law.</skos:definition>
