  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R9v49XBtDD1H7m9vlSsdljw">
    <skos:definition>An Escrow Provisions Clause is a legal provision within an Escrow Clause that outlines the specific terms and conditions for holding funds or property in a neutral third-party account until certain conditions are met.</skos:definition>
