    <rdfs:label>Territorial Market Segment</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:definition>A territorial market segment refers to a group of consumers or businesses categorized based on the geographical boundaries or territories within which they operate. This segmentation allows companies to tailor their marketing strategies and product offerings to the specific characteristics and needs of different countries, regions, or localities.</skos:definition>
