  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/hEH6udu7TNmUfBVfY7yWQQ">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/BPceootDSmSNz2Nt6FtVuA"/>
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://www.naics.com/six-digit-naics/?code=321114"/>
    <rdfs:label>Wood Preservation</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition>This U.S. industry comprises establishments primarily engaged in (1) treating wood sawed, planed, or shaped in other establishments with creosote or other preservatives, such as alkaline copper quat, copper azole, and sodium borates, to prevent decay and to protect against fire and insects and/or (2) sawing round wood poles, pilings, and posts and treating them with preservatives.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
