  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RDrdvM2UI4EaC7URSea35Iu">
    <skos:definition>A Litigation Finance Company is a specialized financial institution that provides funding to plaintiffs or law firms to cover legal costs in exchange for a share of any potential recovery or settlement from a lawsuit.</skos:definition>
