    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:definition>An Obstructed License Plate Claim involves allegations that a vehicle's license plate was not clearly visible or was intentionally obscured, violating traffic regulations that require license plates to be unobstructed and legible. Such claims are essential for ensuring that vehicles can be properly identified by law enforcement and traffic cameras, and they often result in fines or corrective orders.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label>Obstructed License Plate Claim</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
