    <rdfs:label>Voting Rights</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition>Voting rights refer to the legal entitlement that enables eligible citizens to participate in the electoral process to choose their representatives in government. These rights are commonly protected by national constitutions and international treaties like the Universal Declaration of Human Rights, and may include provisions to prevent discrimination based on race, gender, or other factors.</skos:definition>
